            {
              "title": "Present Simple for Routines",
              "weight": 4,
              "content": [
                {
                  "order": 1,
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "{\"time\":1700007004000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yY5zZ6aA7b\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"We use the <b>Present Simple</b> tense to talk about routines — things we do every day.\"}},{\"id\":\"bB8cC9dD0e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Form:</b>\"}},{\"id\":\"eE1fF2gG3h\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"I / You / We / They + verb: <em>I <b>wake</b> up at 7.</em>\",\"He / She / It + verb + <b>s/es</b>: <em>She <b>wakes</b> up at 7.</em>\"]}},{\"id\":\"hH4iI5jJ6k\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Negative:</b>\"}},{\"id\":\"kK7lL8mM9n\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"I <b>don't</b> eat breakfast. / She <b>doesn't</b> eat breakfast.\"]}},{\"id\":\"nN0oO1pP2q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Question:</b>\"}},{\"id\":\"qQ3rR4sS5t\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>Do</b> you eat breakfast? / <b>Does</b> she eat breakfast?\"]}},{\"id\":\"tT6uU7vV8w\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<em>Remember: Add <b>-s</b> or <b>-es</b> for he/she/it!</em>\"}},{\"id\":\"wW9xX0yY1z\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"go → go<b>es</b>, wash → wash<b>es</b>, eat → eat<b>s</b>\"]}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
                },
                {
                  "order": 2,
                  "type": "audio",
                  "content": {
                    "text": "She wakes up at seven. He goes to school every day.",
                    "type": "tts",
                    "audio_url": ""
