        {
          "title": "Talking About Frequency",
          "weight": 6,
          "content": [
            {
              "order": 1,
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{\"time\":1700007006000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"jJ1kK2lL3m\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"We use <b>frequency adverbs</b> to say how often we do things:\"}},{\"id\":\"mM4nN5oO6p\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>always</b> — всегда (100%)\",\"<b>usually</b> — обычно (80%)\",\"<b>often</b> — часто (60%)\",\"<b>sometimes</b> — иногда (40%)\",\"<b>rarely / seldom</b> — редко (20%)\",\"<b>never</b> — никогда (0%)\"]}},{\"id\":\"pP7qQ8rR9s\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Position:</b> The adverb comes <b>before</b> the main verb:\"}},{\"id\":\"sS0tT1uU2v\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"I <b>always</b> wake up early.\",\"She <b>sometimes</b> skips breakfast.\",\"He <b>never</b> goes to bed late.\"]}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
            },
            {
              "order": 2,
              "type": "audio",
              "content": {
                "text": "I always eat breakfast. She sometimes goes shopping. He never goes to bed late.",
                "type": "tts",
